            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, I am afraid luarocks support out of the box is not planned. Mostly for complexity reasons.\r\n\r\nThere are [various hooks](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/73bbcbfa7839c4b00a64965fb504f87461abefbd/doc/mini-deps.txt#L278-L289) for users to take advantage of. Actual way of utilizing that (how to make sure that proper rocks are installed) is also left to users. Maybe a custom `vim.system()` call will be enough?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No, I am afraid luarocks support out of the box is not planned. Mostly for complexity reasons.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/73bbcbfa7839c4b00a64965fb504f87461abefbd/doc/mini-deps.txt#L278-L289\">various hooks</a> for users to take advantage of. Actual way of utilizing that (how to make sure that proper rocks are installed) is also left to users. Maybe a custom <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.system()</code> call will be enough?</p>",
            "bodyText": "No, I am afraid luarocks support out of the box is not planned. Mostly for complexity reasons.\nThere are various hooks for users to take advantage of. Actual way of utilizing that (how to make sure that proper rocks are installed) is also left to users. Maybe a custom vim.system() call will be enough?",
