                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> However, now when I do `DepsClean`, the `luarocks` directory would always appear in the list. Is there a way to always ignore a particular directory, or I would need to move the luarocks packages tree to other places?\r\n\r\nI'd suggest using some other path, because both 'pack/deps/opt' and 'pack/deps/start' are special. My suggestion would be either 'pack/deps' directly, some other optional package directory ('pack/luarocks/opt', 'pack/luarocks/start', 'pack/luarocks'), or indeed another subdirectory of standard path. I'd prefer trying in that same order until it works (probably all should work).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, now when I do <code class=\"notranslate\">DepsClean</code>, the <code class=\"notranslate\">luarocks</code> directory would always appear in the list. Is there a way to always ignore a particular directory, or I would need to move the luarocks packages tree to other places?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd suggest using some other path, because both 'pack/deps/opt' and 'pack/deps/start' are special. My suggestion would be either 'pack/deps' directly, some other optional package directory ('pack/luarocks/opt', 'pack/luarocks/start', 'pack/luarocks'), or indeed another subdirectory of standard path. I'd prefer trying in that same order until it works (probably all should work).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "However, now when I do DepsClean, the luarocks directory would always appear in the list. Is there a way to always ignore a particular directory, or I would need to move the luarocks packages tree to other places?\n\nI'd suggest using some other path, because both 'pack/deps/opt' and 'pack/deps/start' are special. My suggestion would be either 'pack/deps' directly, some other optional package directory ('pack/luarocks/opt', 'pack/luarocks/start', 'pack/luarocks'), or indeed another subdirectory of standard path. I'd prefer trying in that same order until it works (probably all should work).",
